            "answer": {
              "short": "The triangles below and above the $x$-axis have equal areas, so their signed areas cancel.",
              "worked": "The triangle on $[0,1]$ lies below the $x$-axis, and the triangle on $[1,2]$ lies above it. Both have base $1$ and height $1$, so their areas are equal. Their signed areas cancel, giving $\\displaystyle\\int_0^2(x-1)\\,dx=0$.",
